{"resourceIdentifier":"953","resourceName":"The Paraguay Forest Conservation Project - Reduction of GHG emissions from deforestation and forest degradation in the Chaco-Pantanal ecosystem","description":"The project consists of the purchase and protection of 4,745 ha of forested land with High Conservation Values in the eastern Chaco-Pantanal transition zone in Alto Paraguay, threatened in the absence of the project with transformation into cattle ranching. The project goal is to conserve the natural and cultural values of the area, including its sequestered carbon. Climate benefits are achieved by preventing deforestation.Ownership and management of the area is shared between a Paraguayan biodiversity conservation NGO (Guyra Paraguay) and the Yshir indigenous community (represented by the Unión de Comunidades de la Nación Yshir or UCINY), with legal safeguards to ensure permanence of conservation management regime. The project is also submitted for CCBA validation.This is an initial project instance of a grouped project. Other instances are envisaged, replicating the same pattern.PUBLIC COMMENT PERIOD:This project was open for public comment from 01 November - 01 December 2019. 1)CCB_MONIT_REP_SUM_ESP_DRAFT_953_25FEB2013_24FEB20182)CCB_MONIT_REP_ENG_DRAFT_953_25FEB2013_24FEB2018","location":{"latitude":-20.967034,"longitude":-58.976599},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-05-14","endExclusive":"2021-06-14","endInclusive":"2021-06-13"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"953"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Districts of Bahia Negra and Fuerte Olimpo"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Swire Pacific Offshore Operations (Pte) Ltd. (SPO)"},{"type":"string","value":"Singapore, Singapore"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":